//// Decision 535 — an uncaught `@panic` writes `panic: <message>` to stderr on
//// every target: the `Failure` an `attempt` would have answered, `<kind>:
//// <message>`, never the runtime's own report (node's stack trace, erlang's
//// raw term). What was printed before stays printed; nothing after it runs.

pub fn main() {
    val text = "boom";
    @print("before");
    @panic(text);
    @print("after");
}
